  "slug": "artist:2-unlimited",
  "name": "2 Unlimited",
  "editorial_article": "Founded in 1991 in Antwerp, Belgium, by producers Jean-Paul De Coster and Phil Wilde, 2 Unlimited rose to global prominence as a seminal Eurodance act. The project initially featured an instrumental foundation before incorporating the vocals of Ray Slijngaard and Anita Doth. Their breakthrough hit, 'Get Ready for This', reached the top ten in multiple countries, eventually charting on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100 three years after its initial 1991 release. Across their career, they secured sixteen international hits, including the chart-topping 'No Limit', which achieved platinum certification in Germany. Despite facing criticism from the British press, the duo maintained a dominant presence in dance music, winning three consecutive World Music Awards for Best-Selling Benelux Artist between 1993 and 1995. Following the departure of Doth and Slijngaard in 1996, De Coster continued the project with various vocalists, eventually reuniting with the original members in 2012 for live performances and updated remixes.",
